 "blockers": [],
 "notes": [
  "Result values (best, average, attempts, record values) are integers in centiseconds: 981 = 9.81 s. For 333fm, a single is a move count and an average is moves*100. 333mbf values are encoded multi-blind scores. -1 means DNF, -2 means DNS, 0 means no attempt.",
  "Round type ids: 1/2/3 = first/second/third round, f = final, c = combined final, d = combined first round. Format ids: a = average of 5, m = mean of 3, 1/2/3 = best of N.",
  "Event ids: 333, 222, 444, 555, 666, 777, 333bf, 333fm, 333oh, clock, minx, pyram, skewb, sq1, 444bf, 555bf, 333mbf. Get a competition's own event list from get-competition-wcif or the event_ids field in competition listings.",
  "search-competitions mirrors the web UI. Pass today's date as ongoing_and_future to get only upcoming/ongoing competitions; omit it to include past ones. For past competitions in a date range, list-competitions with start/end is more reliable.",
  "The HTML pages /persons/{id}, /results/rankings and /results/records return 403 to non-browser clients; use the /api/v0 commands instead. robots.txt disallows /search and /api/v0/search/users.",
  "Everything here is public and read-only; no login is needed. The cookie-banner acknowledgement POST was skipped on purpose."
 ],
